23:["$","section","the-outbrick-loop",{"id":"the-outbrick-loop","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The OutBrick loop is intentionally small"}],[["$","p","OutBrick starts with a board that can be understood at a glance. You do not need to remember a quest log, manage a stamina meter, or wait for a timer to expire. The board tells you what matters: the bricks, the open lanes, and the matching gates.",{"children":"OutBrick starts with a board that can be understood at a glance. You do not need to remember a quest log, manage a stamina meter, or wait for a timer to expire. The board tells you what matters: the bricks, the open lanes, and the matching gates."}],["$","p","Undo is part of the loop rather than a punishment for using it. That changes the emotional temperature of experimentation. You can try a move, learn from the result, and keep the useful part of the attempt. The goal is not to make every board effortless; it is to make curiosity safer than hesitation.",{"children":"Undo is part of the loop rather than a punishment for using it. That changes the emotional temperature of experimentation. You can try a move, learn from the result, and keep the useful part of the attempt. The goal is not to make every board effortless; it is to make curiosity safer than hesitation."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"article-bullets","children":[["$","li","One readable board at a time",{"children":"One readable board at a time"}],["$","li","A clear action-to-feedback relationship",{"children":"A clear action-to-feedback relationship"}],["$","li","Recovery tools that preserve curiosity",{"children":"Recovery tools that preserve curiosity"}],["$","li","A finish line that arrives before the session feels heavy",{"children":"A finish line that arrives before the session feels heavy"}]]}],null,null]}]
24:["$","section","take-the-good-bit-with-you",{"id":"take-the-good-bit-with-you","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Take the good bit with you"}],[["$","p","The best two-minute session is not the one that keeps you captive. It is the one that gives you a small feeling of progress and lets you decide what happens next. If you have time for another board, there is always another board. If you need to go, the game can wait.",{"children":"The best two-minute session is not the one that keeps you captive. It is the one that gives you a small feeling of progress and lets you decide what happens next. If you have time for another board, there is always another board. If you need to go, the game can wait."}],["$","p","That is why OutBrick treats calm as a design input. The research does not say every player benefits in the same way, and it does not prove a universal effect. It does suggest a useful north star: build a game that respects agency, makes progress legible, and leaves the player with more choice than they had before.",{"children":"That is why OutBrick treats calm as a design input. The research does not say every player benefits in the same way, and it does not prove a universal effect. It does suggest a useful north star: build a game that respects agency, makes progress legible, and leaves the player with more choice than they had before."}]],null,null,["$","p",null,{"className":"article-source-note","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Research trail"}],[["$","a","motivation-2010",{"href":"#reference-motivation-2010","aria-label":"Jump to source: Przybylski, Rigby, & Ryan (2010)","children":["[",1,"]"]}],["$","a","time-wellbeing-2022",{"href":"#reference-time-wellbeing-2022","aria-label":"Jump to source: Vuorre et al. (2022)","children":["[",5,"]"]}]]]}]]}]
